  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It builds a 260×260 ground plane and 10,000 instanced objects: 8,000 trees (an instanced cylinder trunk and an instanced cone canopy, 16,000 instances in all) and 2,000 rocks (instanced flattened spheres). Placement uses a fixed-seed LCG within a radius of 75. Canopies get per-instance HSL green variation and rocks get per-instance grey-brown variation, on white base materials. The scene has one shadow-casting directional light plus a hemisphere fill, and `effects.fog` with mode \"exp\". The camera is `camera.orbit` with `autoRotate` 0.08 rad/s, positioned at [0, 85, 125] so the whole forest is in view. `__EVAL_READY__` is set after `await app.ready()` and one rAF. Typecheck passes. I couldn't run it in a browser, so the visuals are untested. That includes the camera orbit, the fog density, the shadow coverage and whether `window.__EVAL_READY__` gets set.",
